name: Nested manifest policy signals retain inspection gaps through Review, Report and restart
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dependency_hygiene.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: run dep-hygiene:check {}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 Incomplete inspection | nested-partial
expect: second/package.json
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dependency_hygiene.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | inspection-reader
resize: 160x48
live-snap: inspection-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: inspection-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: inspection-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: inspection-60x20
resize: 40x12
keys: End
live-snap: inspection-40x12-tail
keys: PPage
live-snap: inspection-40x12-page-1
keys: PPage
live-snap: inspection-40x12-page-2
keys: PPage
live-snap: inspection-40x12-page-3
keys: PPage
live-snap: inspection-40x12-page-4
keys: PPage
live-snap: inspection-40x12-page-5
ask: Are actual inspected/discovered counts, limits, exclusions and invalid nested manifest reachable at all six sizes without implying known vulnerability verification or full coverage?
keys: q
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape C-u
paste-file: @ART/scan-command.txt
keys: Enter
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 30 Partial dep-hygiene: | shared-scan-partial
expect: second/package.json
expect-not: prerequisite chain aborted after sast:scan failed
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dependency_hygiene.py @TMP_TARGET @ART scanned
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 signal-only | first-policy-finding
submit: decision deferred Owned manifest policy requires owner review
require-live-snap: 25 Owned manifest policy | first-deferred
submit: open F-0002
require-live-snap: 25 signal-only | second-policy-finding
submit: decision deferred Owned manifest policy requires owner review
require-live-snap: 25 Owned manifest policy | second-deferred
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Enter export | report
keys: s j j j Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dependency_hygiene.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
ask: Do real nested and root observations retain their paths, signal-only status and scripted deferrals in the report while SAST preserves the invalid manifest gap?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 30 Owned manifest policy | restarted-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dependency_hygiene.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain both source-qualified policy findings, deferrals and partial inspection receipts without another scan, provider request or package installation?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
